WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.250
A voltmeter has two leads.

2
00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:06.070
It can only ever measure the
difference between two points.

3
00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:10.210
A cell is built from two halves,
each with its own electrode.

4
00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:14.790
So how could you ever measure the
voltage of just one half, on its own?

5
00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:17.290
How can you measure the
voltage of half a battery,

6
00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:20.110
when a voltmeter needs two connections?

7
00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:23.330
In this mission, you'll set up
the standard hydrogen electrode,

8
00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:26.860
and measure the standard
electrode potential of nickel.

9
00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:29.730
You'll read a table of
standard electrode potentials,

10
00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:33.390
and use it to rank oxidizing
and reducing agents.

11
00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:38.030
Your mission: explain how the voltage
of a single half-cell can be measured.
